151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Bearings are critical components in countless mechanical systems, from industrial machinery and automobiles to aerospace and energy sectors. They support rotating shafts, reduce friction, and ensure smooth operation. If a fault occurs in the system, it can severely affect the process, increasing its bottleneck affecting productivity and safety. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Vibrations play a crucial role in analyzing the health and performance of rotating machinery, Rotating components can increase vibrations in a system. While some level of vibration is inevitable and normal, excessive or irregular vibrations often indicate underlying mechanical issues, such as misalignment or imbalance occurring due to spalling, pitting or minute cracks. Understanding these vibrations and delving into its causes can help increase the efficiency of our system. Stator current responses can directly indicate faults in a mechanical system. One of the most common types of faults in the system arises from bearing failures. Predicting these faults can have a significant impact on system reliability, efficiency, and maintenance costs. Early detection of bearing faults allows for early maintenance ensuring safety.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
