179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (While MCSA is traditionally used for motor fault detection, its application to bearings coupled with shafts, as explored in the research, is highly relevant to our project. The research demonstrates that faults in bearings can affect the torque and the current signature of the motor, leading to characteristic modulations in the stator current. This insight allows us to consider MCSA as a potential diagnostic tool for detecting faults in bearings coupled to shafts, without the need for complex and expensive vibration sensors. MCSA offers a non-intrusive, cost-effective solution, especially beneficial in systems where vibration sensors might be difficult to install or maintain.)
/E (While MCSA is traditionally used for motor fault detection, its application to bearings coupled with shafts, as explored in the research, is highly relevant to our project. The research demonstrates that faults in bearings can affect the torque and the current signature of the motor, leading to characteristic modulations in the stator current. This insight allows us to consider MCSA as a potential diagnostic tool for detecting faults in bearings coupled to shafts, without the need for complex and expensive vibration sensors. MCSA offers a non-intrusive, cost-effective solution, especially beneficial in systems where vibration sensors might be difficult to install or maintain.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
