/T (Frequency Spectrum \(Vibration Signature\) of a Healthy and Faulty Bearing The plot shows amplitude \(g\) versus frequency \(Hz\), illustrating the frequency components of vibrations in both a healthy and faulty bearing. The peaks in the spectrum indicate dominant vibration frequencies, with additional peaks at characteristic fault frequencies associated with the outer race fault \(ORF\). The two curves \(B1 and B2\) correspond to different conditions \(healthy vs. faulty\), showing how fault-induced vibrations introduce additional frequency components.)
/E (Frequency Spectrum \(Vibration Signature\) of a Healthy and Faulty Bearing The plot shows amplitude \(g\) versus frequency \(Hz\), illustrating the frequency components of vibrations in both a healthy and faulty bearing. The peaks in the spectrum indicate dominant vibration frequencies, with additional peaks at characteristic fault frequencies associated with the outer race fault \(ORF\). The two curves \(B1 and B2\) correspond to different conditions \(healthy vs. faulty\), showing how fault-induced vibrations introduce additional frequency components.)
