230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Healthy vs Faulty Bearings: The amplitude of the fundamental running frequency \(35 Hz\) and its harmonics are higher for faulty bearings compared to healthy ones. This indicates that bearing faults introduce anomalies in the current signal due to rotor displacement relative to the stator.)
/E (Healthy vs Faulty Bearings: The amplitude of the fundamental running frequency \(35 Hz\) and its harmonics are higher for faulty bearings compared to healthy ones. This indicates that bearing faults introduce anomalies in the current signal due to rotor displacement relative to the stator.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Characteristic Fault Frequencies: Faults produce impulses at characteristic frequencies related to bearing geometry and rotor speed. These frequencies manifest as sidebands around the running frequency in the current spectrum, which are reliable indicators of bearing defects. The induction motor acts as a transducer, reflecting load variations caused by bearing faults in its stator current spectrum. By monitoring current harmonics and analyzing sidebands using techniques like FFT and wavelet scalograms, the study effectively distinguishes between healthy and faulty bearings installed in mechanical systems driven by an induction motor.)
/E (Characteristic Fault Frequencies: Faults produce impulses at characteristic frequencies related to bearing geometry and rotor speed. These frequencies manifest as sidebands around the running frequency in the current spectrum, which are reliable indicators of bearing defects. The induction motor acts as a transducer, reflecting load variations caused by bearing faults in its stator current spectrum. By monitoring current harmonics and analyzing sidebands using techniques like FFT and wavelet scalograms, the study effectively distinguishes between healthy and faulty bearings installed in mechanical systems driven by an induction motor.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
