385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In conclusion, this project successfully demonstrates the development of an intelligent fault detection system for mechanical systems, with a primary focus on identifying bearing faults through vibration and Motor Current Signature Analysis \(MCSA\). By analyzing frequency-domain characteristics and current signature variations, we established a reliable foundation for diagnosing bearing defects, particularly in outer rings. Machine learning models were developed and evaluated to enhance the diagnostic process, with the Decision Tree model achieving the highest accuracy at 96.0%, followed by the Artificial Neural Network \(ANN\) at 94.0%, and the Support Vector Machine \(SVM\) at 88.0%. These results highlight the effectiveness of ML in fault classification and automation. Looking ahead, these models will be integrated into a real-time predictive maintenance framework to enable early fault detection, reduce unplanned downtimes, and improve overall system reliability. This project lays a strong foundation for the implementation of smarter, data-driven maintenance strategies in industrial environments.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
